\section{Give Storage, Meaning, and Identity Separate Names}

An instruction's bit pattern need not contain its operands in the form an execution unit, compiler, or programmer uses them. A VADL \texttt{format} describes the bit layout and any derived operands. An \texttt{encoding} sets the constant values that identify a particular instruction. Its \texttt{instruction} body defines the operation over the resulting operands. Separating these three lets instructions share a layout without sharing either their operation or their identifying constants. This chapter uses Sections~3.3 and~4.5 of the February 2024 VADL preprint, arXiv:2402.09087v1 \cite{himmelbauer2024vadl}.

Listing~3 illustrates width-based layout: the declarations of the I-type fields, from the first twelve-bit immediate to the final seven-bit opcode, occupy adjacent bits in order from high to low. Listing~2 illustrates explicit positions, necessary when an encoded value is scattered. This excerpt from Listing~2 preserves VADL syntax, normalizing spacing:

\begin{verbatim}
format Btype : Inst =
  { imm    [31, 7, 30..25, 11..8]
  , rs2    [24..20]
  , rs1    [19..15]
  , funct3 [14..12]
  , opcode [6..0]
  , immS = (imm as SInt<Size1>, 0b0) : predicate {
      immS => (immS(0) = 0) & (((immS as UInt) + 4096) <= 8191)
    } : encode {
      imm => immS(12..1)
    }
  }
\end{verbatim}

With a 32-bit \texttt{Inst} and \texttt{Size1} equal to 31, the cast and concatenation turn a 12-bit stored value into a signed, even byte displacement represented in 32 bits. The predicate accepts from \(-4096\) through \(4094\) in steps of two. The inverse packs displacement bits 12 through 1, omitting the known-zero bit 0. Test the predicate before dropping any bits: otherwise an input of \(+4096\) can appear to fit after being turned into the encoding for \(-4096\).

\section{Read a Split Field in the Written Order}

\Cref{fig:visual-325} shows the significant ordering: instruction bit 7 is not adjacent to bit 31 in the stored word, but the two become neighbors in the assembled immediate. An implementation can represent the format as a list of slices with destination positions. Then the same mapping can be used in reverse for emission, without a second manually maintained list of shifts. Endianness determines how the word is serialized to memory; neither big- nor little-endian serialization renumbers the bits of the resulting word.

